convincing|Persuasive appearance is distinguished from factual truth. Payment context matches the adjective; Vietnamese preserves epistemic caution and grammar makes no tense restriction.
exercise|Four source-supported boundaries separate physical activity, the intransitive verb, a countable practice task and formal use of rights. Examples and Vietnamese match each POS and valency.
law|Rule and legal field remain distinct noun proposals; the example asserts only a fictional rule, not current legal advice. Countability and article use match each sense; rights remain unresolved.
participation|Workshop participation is voluntary involvement rather than attendance permission as a lexical rule. Vietnamese sentence naturally expresses open participation; in/by constructions and uncountability checked.
shelter|Protection as noun and transitive protection as verb are separate. The barn sentence preserves the storm and hikers; from wind valency is supported and no separate approved identity is inferred.
